<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">20 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 20 November, from 1272 to 1945.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/scotland" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/scotland.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1272 <span class="tih-ago">754 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward I is proclaimed king while returning from crusade</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Four days after Henry III's death, his son Edward was proclaimed king though still abroad. Edward I conquered Wales, expelled England's Jews in 1290 and waged long wars against Scotland.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1759 <span class="tih-ago">267 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hawke defeats the French fleet at Quiberon Bay</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a gale off Brittany, Admiral Edward Hawke pursued the French fleet among the rocks and shoals of Quiberon Bay and destroyed or scattered it. The victory ended French plans to invade Britain.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1820 <span class="tih-ago">206 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A sperm whale sinks the whaleship Essex</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the South Pacific, an enraged sperm whale rammed and sank the Nantucket whaleship Essex. Survivors spent about three months in open boats, resorting to cannibalism; the story inspired Moby-Dick.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1917 <span class="tih-ago">109 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British tanks attack in mass at Cambrai</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 476 British tanks led a surprise attack at Cambrai, breaking through German lines several miles in a day. A German counter-attack soon recovered most of the ground, but the tactics pointed to the future.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nuremberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1945 <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Nuremberg trials begin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The International Military Tribunal opened at Nuremberg to try 22 senior Nazi leaders for war crimes, crimes against peace and crimes against humanity. The trial laid foundations for international criminal law.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a></div></div></li></ol>
